   <dc:description>
    <rdf:Alt>
     <rdf:li xml:lang="x-default">LONDON - APRIL 18:  Journalist's goodie bags containing a silver birch tree sapling await collection before Conservative party leader David Cameron's press conference on 'green' issues on April 18, 2006 in London.This final phase of local election campaigning coincides with the publication of a pamphlet committing the Conservatives to a 'new green revolution' in Britain . Mr Cameron stated that Conservative councils have the highest average of recycling and composting.  (Photo by Peter Macdiarmid/Getty Images)</rdf:li>
    </rdf:Alt>
